ng the  impression that the world had already  ended leaving Sonora with only the  company of her memories the story takes  a sympathetic approach to portraying  mental illness and isn't at all  interested in showing the differences  between reality and imagination it's all  about cinemas perspective and with their  visions and was truly real being  presented as one in the same on our  journey through the cursed lands Senna  will utilize her skills in combat to  fight an army of berserkers that appear  out of thin air with fast heavy sword  swings as well as up-close hand-to-hand  strikes he'll hack away at your foes  while dodging and paring their strikes  to get the upper hand these combat  sequences are intense and offer the most  thrilling moments of the game  combats true challenge and satisfaction  come from mastering the base combat  mechanics which is fluid and responsive  allowing you to bounce between multiple  foes easily with their inner voices  warning you of incoming strikes the  intrusive inner voices are easily the  most oppressive aspect of cinema  psychosis using binaural audio making  headphones a must for the full effect  you'll experience what it's like to have  several voices in your head into the  mountain can you see it shall we tell  how where to go  [Music]  in many ways it feels like a subversive  take on the common video game trope with  the bodyless companion offering help be  a radio making them a somewhat  distressing presence you desperately  want to keep at arm's length the  effectiveness of the inner voices and  making you uncomfortable is a testament  to the stellar presentation of the game  which uses some rather inventive tricks  to manipulate cinemas perspective and in  turn your own it does well to make you  feel on edge and in a state of confusion  while simultaneously getting you to  focus on the more tangible and true  elements of our surroundings even if  they are still hallucinations the voices  however can be a boon to yo